   132	Nevertheless it is not globally monogenic.  Give `x,y` weights `2,1`.
   133	The cases `s=0` or `t=0` are immediate.  Otherwise let `p,q` be their weighted degrees and `s_p,t_q` their
   134	top parts.  If `p>q`, the unique top term of `I(s,t)` is `xs_p^3`; if
   135	`q>p`, it is `y^2t_q^3`.  If `p=q`, the top part is
   136	
   137	```text
