   142	a cube in `C(x,y)`.  Hence `I(s,t)` is never a nonzero constant.  This is
   143	a genuinely global failure: (2.1) is primitive at every maximal ideal
   144	(the middle coefficients are nonzero constants), and over the infinite
   145	residue field one can choose a residue vector on which it is nonzero;
   146	the algebra is therefore locally monogenic everywhere.
   147	
   148	This example disproves any theorem deduced only from “UFD, all projectives
   149	free, locally monogenic, connected normal cubic algebra, irreducible reduced sextic
   150	discriminant, generic group `S_3`.”  It is not a counterexample to the
   151	charged row: the leading form of (2.2) is `x^2y^4`, so its projective
