   177	For the physical sextic `c!=0`.  Choose a linear form `M` independent of
   178	`L`, put `t=M/L`, and set `alpha(t)=A/L^2`, `beta(t)=B/L^3`.  These are
   179	polynomials of degrees at most two and three satisfying
   180	`4alpha^3+27beta^2=c`.  They are coprime.  Differentiation gives
   181	
   182	```text
   183	2alpha^2 alpha' + 9beta beta' = 0.
   184	```
   185	
   186	Consequently `alpha^2 | beta'` and `beta | alpha'`.  If their positive
   187	degrees are `m,n`, this would give `2m<=n-1` and `n<=m-1`, an impossibility.
   188	If either is constant, (3.1) makes the other constant.  Thus all and only the
