where V ≥ 0 is the sum of possible contribution from all the other ramification points. It
follows that V = 0. In other words, the covering J is unramified outside 0, 1, ∞ and also
at J −1 (∞) − {∞}. This proves (c1) ⇒ (c2).
      The converse is obvious.
